\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  shilling nudges higher on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2008\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Sept 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shilling firmed slightly against the dollar on Friday, thanks to talk in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem further falls, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 At 1058 GMT, commercial banks posted the unit at 70.40/50 against the dollar compared with Thursday's close of 70.80/90.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the unit was likely to stay stable at around 70.50/60 in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 "There was some material news which hit the market after it closed on Thursday. There was an attempt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Chris Muiga, a senior dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  Commercial Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said the regulator offered to sell dollars to stop the unit's slide. It had not, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the end.\par \par \uc2 The shilling has been losing ground for the last week on heavy demand for greenbacks from importers.\par \par \uc2 "There is a feeling in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be happy with a weak shilling, so I think it will be anchored around 70.50/60," said Muiga.\par \par \uc2 James Ndegwa, an \uc2 Imperial Bank\uc2  trader, also said the unit was likely to stay stable.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  <KES=> <KES1