\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  props Uganda, Tanzania shillings  \b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2006\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, May 31 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  shilling <KES=> held steady against the dollar, while the Tanzanian <TZS=> and Ugandan <UGX=> \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to be propped up by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the week to Wednesday, dealers said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 KENYA\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  shilling held steady against the dollar in the week to Wednesday. At 1125 GMT the shilling traded at 72.05/25 to the dollar, compared with last Wednesday's close of 72.00/10.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling initially strengthened to touch 71.60/80 to the dollar as banks sold off the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then it weakened to touch 72.50/60 to the dollar, undermined by importers demand.  \par \par \uc2 "It has been quite volatile. We experienced a bit of turbulence," said Peter Njuguna, of Commercial Bank of Africa.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling has since regained ground, lifted by dollar inflows and as banks took profits, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Initially people took long positions, anticipating end month demand, but as we came into this week there was not much demand and we've seen interbank players sell into the market," said a dealer at Barclays Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expect the shilling to trade in the 71.75-72.60 range against the dollar in coming days, with a bias for it to hover around 72.00.  \par \par \uc2 UGANDA  \par \par \uc2 The Ugandan shilling weakened against the dollar, undermined by increased dollar demand from banks and corporate clients, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented further losses.  \par \par \uc2 At 1100 GMT commercial banks quoted the shilling at 1,848/1,853 to the dollar, compared with 1,835/1,840 at last Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 "We have seen the shilling slide lower against the dollar due to increased corporate demand mainly from the telecommunication sector and the interbank market," Catherine Kijjaggulwi, a dealer at Barclays Bank, said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Wednesday, putting brakes on the shilling's weakening.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the sale side mainly to smoothen out depreciation of the shilling," said David Bagambe, chief dealer at DFCU Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers forecast the shilling will continue to depreciate in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close the week at 1,855 levels.  \par \par \uc2 "Anticipated end-month inflows are too weak to meet the surge in dollar demand in the market. Unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with substantial amounts to prop the shilling, the market will continue to see it slide," Bagambe said.  \par \par \uc2 TANZANIA  \par \par \uc2 The Tanzania shilling <TZS=> firmed marginally against the dollar in the week to Wednesday, amid increased demand from the telecoms and energy sectors, buoyed by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 At 0935 GMT the local unit traded at 1,247/1,257 to the dollar, compared with last Wednesday's close of 1,250/1,258, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 During the week, the shilling weakened to levels of 1,255/1,265, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Tanzania (BOT) came to the market to sell the dollar at 1,250 shillings.  \par \par \uc2 "There was high demand for the dollar, especially from the telecoms and the oil sector. The demand could not match the supply," said Rose Mollel, a senior dealer at CRDB Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that BOT \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times during the week.  \par \par \uc2 "This has been the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming to the market and selling dollars at very low prices from where the market was," said Samwuel Marco, a dealer at Stanbic Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expect the shilling to continue gaining against the dollar, boosted by BOT's continued presence in the market, and by corporate clients selling dollars to meet their shilling-denominated end-month payments.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EAST AFRICA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|AFN|RBN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF|SXNA  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060603e25v000a2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
