\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya anti-graft body says probed c.bank governor  \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 18:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, March 7 (Reuters) - The Kenya anti-corruption agency said on Tuesday it had investigated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Andrew Mullei over corruption allegations and forwarded its recommendations to the attorney general for action.  \par \par \uc2 "We did receive some complaints, allegations, which we did investigate some time back," Nicholas Simani, the spokesman of the Kenya Anti-Corruption Commission (KACC) told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "We came up with specific recommendations which we forwarded to the attorney general for appropriate action," he added but refused to divulge details of the recommendations.  \par \par \uc2 Kenya's tabloids have repeatedly carried stories accusing Mullei of nepotism and corruption at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Standard, one of Kenya's leading newspapers, reported on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  had asked KACC to investigate Mullei over allegations of corruption.  \par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the governor's office.  \par \par \uc2 The Standard said KACC had received the letter from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Feb. 27 and had not acted on it. But Simani said KACC had completed its own investigations on the governor on Feb 23.  \par \par \uc2 The anti-graft body has no powers to prosecute which are vested in the office of the attorney general.  \par \par \uc2 The allegations of corruption in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are the latest to rock President Mwai Kibaki's government whose image has suffered badly after three senior ministers resigned over graft.  \par \par \uc2 The finance, energy and education ministers resigned last month after their names were linked to two graft scandals in which millions of state funds were corruptly paid out.  \par \par \uc2 Mullei, who has strongly rejected recent pressure by manufacturers and exporters to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  shilling, has previously faced allegations of wrongdoing over a banknotes printing tender.  \par \par \uc2 He denied any wrongdoing over the tender which was later awarded to Britain's De La Rue \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Mullei was appointed by Kibaki in March 2003. As the governor, he enjoys security of tenure. Under Kenyan laws, the governor can be sacked if convicted of dishonesty or fraud or upon the recommendations of a tribunal appointed by the president to investigate him.  \par \par \uc2 KENYA-CORRUPTION-GOVERNOR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AFN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|G|RNP|DNP|PGE|SXNA  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060307e237001vz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
