\par\par \b \uc2 Traders predict a weaker path for Kenyan shilling.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By George Obulutsa   \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2005\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, April 1 (Reuters) - The Kenya shilling  is expected to fall to a range of 76.00-77.50 to the dollar in the short-term after verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on an anticipated rise in importer demand, analysts said on Friday.    \par \par \uc2  The shilling has risen steadily in recent months, gaining 10 percent since mid-December when it started its latest rally.    \par \par \uc2  It rose to a 21-month high of 72.90/73.10 on March 21, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's competitiveness, warned that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem any speculation on the shilling.    \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the shilling's gains were overdone and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments were the trigger that was needed to reverse the shilling's path.    \par \par \uc2  The unit closed on Thursday at 74.60/80 to the dollar.    \par \par \uc2  "I think the move down to 73.00 was overdone. It was only a matter of time before it reversed. These levels were not sustainable at the end of the day," said Robert Otieno, the treasurer at Stanbic Bank.    \par \par \uc2  Experts say the local unit has been well-supported by dollar receipts from the farm and tourism sectors, strong inflows from non-governmental organisations and investors seeking to purchase high-yield shilling-denominated government bonds.    \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, dollar demand has been severely subdued, with most importers, especially the key oil companies, already hedged and staying on the sidelines as the shilling appreciated.    \par \par \uc2  But dealers and analysts said the shilling's previous pattern suggests that the unit is headed lower and importers are just about to return to the market.    \par \par \uc2  NET IMPORT ECONOMY    \par \par \uc2  "The shilling is going to see some weakness because cyclically we are about due for that kind of weakening and even structurally, with a net import economy, you would generally tend to have a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kihara Maina, the treasurer at Barclays Bank of Kenya. "I see a consolidation around the 76, the 77 level."    \par \par \uc2  OIL PRICES    \par \par \uc2  Analysts said higher oil prices are also expected to exert pressure on the local unit. Oil surged back above $55 a barrel on Thursday and analysts said prices could rise further.    \par \par \uc2  "The $50 a barrel is still a lot for an oil-importing country like Kenya and that suggests that it is unlikely that the shilling would be able to hold on to its strengths indefinitely," Razia Khan, Standard Chartered Bank's chief Africa economist.    \par \par \uc2  "Despite the near-term strength in the shilling we think 77.50 in a few weeks time is still a possibility and then gradually weakening beyond that," she told Reuters from London.    \par \par \uc2  Although higher interest rates - at 8.67 percent - were a key factor supporting the shilling, an aggressive interest rate hike in the U.S. could pressure the Kenyan unit, analysts said.    \par \par \uc2  "Kenyan interest rates would have to be somewhat higher with the Fed continuing to hike rates so that yields attraction will remain in place," Khan said.    \par \par \uc2  The market had its eyes fixed on the outcome of a two-week visit by a mission from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) currently in the country to review its programme.    \par \par \uc2  "I think obviously people are waiting to see what happens when the current negotiations between the...IMF, who are around, and the government to see whether they are releasing aid to Kenya," Otieno said.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050401e141006er\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
