\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling falls after c.bank comments.  \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, March 29 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling\par weakened against the dollar in early trade on Tuesday as the\par market reacted to comments by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that it would\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop any speculation in the market, dealers said.\par     At 0745 GMT, leading commercial banks were quoting the\par shilling at 74.60/80 to the dollar, compared to Thursday's close\par of 73.25/45.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Andrew Mullei said late on Thursday\par that the bank would take "corrective action" if the firming\par shilling faced speculative pressures and added that he expected\par the unit to weaken in due course as demand for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par increases.\par     The news came after the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market had closed and\par players only reacted to it on Tuesday because the markets\par remained closed on Friday and Monday for Easter holidays.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's largely on the back of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's comment that\par they were prepared to take corrective action on the shilling,\par and basically that happened after that market closed," said\par Anthony Kirui, the head of market making at Barclays Bank.\par  \par     "What we're seeing today is people wishing to cover their\par short positions."\par     The shilling has been on an upward trend in recent weeks and\par rallied to a 21-month high of 72.90/73.10 to the dollar last\par week, prompted by a huge dollar sell-off by banks.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the shilling had been boosted by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 increased demand for shilling-denominated government bonds,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 coupled with subdued demand for dollars at a time when dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflows have been heavy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But some analysts said the shilling's recent gains were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overdone and feared that they could undermine the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 competitiveness of Kenya's export sector.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is the market reaction to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sentiment  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that they will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. The market took a cue  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from that and decided to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  themselves," said Jeremiah  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kendagor, a senior dealer at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Commercial Bank.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We've seen interbank players come into the market to buy  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollars. We've also seen importers come into the market as well  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and buy dollars to meet their obligations," Kirui said, adding  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that he expected the shilling to remain volatile for the rest of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the day.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                   ............Shilling spot rates\par            ...............Shilling forward rates\par                      .Cross rates\par                ............All Kenya Contributors\par               ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par              ......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                            