\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya shilling down slightly as dollar demand rises.  \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Nov 19 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling weakened marginally against the dollar on Friday, as month-end demand started to kick in, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0845 GMT, leading commercial banks in Nairobi posted the rate as 81.30/50 against the dollar, down slightly from the opening of 81.30/45.  \par \par \uc2 "Month-end demand will really kick in from next week. We have been seeing some increase from corporates. That tells me that a lot of them are getting ready to meet their (month-end) obligations," said Bryan Muigai, a trader at Standard Chartered Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been subdued in the last few months, with dealers predicting the shilling would remain in a tight range of 80.90/81.50 in the short term, barring any new market-moving news.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Andrew Mullei, who \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market earlier this year to combat sharp drops in the shilling, said on Tuesday he was comfortable with the current exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 He told Reuters that supply and demand were evenly matched and that fundamentals indicated the rate was where it should be.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par          ............Shilling spot rates\par  ...............Shilling forward rates\par          .Cross rates\par  ............All Kenya Contributors\par  ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par  ......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                    .Treasury bill yields\par  , ..Daily interbank lending rate\par  ...Kenya Bond pricing\par   \f