\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya's shilling weakens on dollar demand.   \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2004\par 09:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling weakened marginally against the dollar in early trading on Thursday as dollar importers began to test the market to meet end-of-the-month demand, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 At 0745 GMT, leading commercial banks in Nairobi posted the rate as 81.20/40 against the dollar, compared with the morning's opening of 81.15/35.   \par \par \uc2 "We have started to see some key interest from large-and medium-scale importers to buy dollars, which has fed into the market and put some pressure on the shilling, as usually happens when we head into the end of the month," said Anthony Kirui, a senior dealer at Barclays Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Moses Kiboi, senior trader at Citibank, said "The dollar will appreciate as we move into month-end demand. The exporters have their bills to pay at the end of the month."   \par \par \uc2 Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been subdued in the last few months, with dealers predicting the shilling will remain in a tight range of 80.90/81.50 in the short term, barring any new market-moving news.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Andrew Mullei, who \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market earlier this year to combat sharp drops in the shilling, on Tuesday said he was comfortable with the current exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 He told Reuters that supply and demand were evenly matched and that fundamentals indicated the rate was where it should be.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          ............Shilling spot rates\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ...............Shilling forward rates    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       