\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling flat vs dlr after c.bank acts.   \b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2004\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Sept 3 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling  was little changed against the U.S. dollar on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again sold the greenback to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.    \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT, leading commercial banks posted the shilling at 80.07/80.27 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , barely changed from Thursday's 80.10/80.30 close.    \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the shilling was under pressure from oil importers and distributors seeking U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay for purchases of refined products, with world petroleum prices near historic highs.    \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand fuelled by high oil import bills helped push the shilling to historic lows of 83.25/45 last month.    \par \par \uc2  Other pressure this week came from a dearth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  receipts from the tea sector, with output and exports depressed by unfavourable weather, said Kennedy Butiko of Bank of Africa \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  On August 26 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the prop up the shilling, blaming its rapid slide on speculation by some market players and saying a rate weaker than 79 shillings could not be explained by fundamentals.    \par \par \uc2  The bank sold dolllars into the market again on Friday. A bank official declined to disclosed the amounts involved.    \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the overall outlook for the shilling was still unsettled, amid jitters over the intentions of international lenders and donors who help fund the government's budget and development proghrammes.    \par \par \uc2  "The underlying sentiment on the shilling's future direction is uncertainty over donor policy," said Moses Kiboi of Citibank.    \par \par \uc2  The shilling took a knock in July when the European Union disclosed it had postponed a decision on an aid package Kenya needs to finance its budget.    \par \par \uc2  The move, a fresh sign of donor impatience with the government's faltering anti-corruption campaign, fuelled fears that donors were considering suspending aid the east African country desperately needs to escape from poverty.    \par \par \uc2  The EU and other top international donors warned Kenya earlier this year that it risked losing vital funding, saying corruption still appeared to be at the heart of government despite President Mwai Kibaki's promises to stamp it out.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          ............Shilling spot rates\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          .Cross rates\par  \par  ............All Kenya Contributors\par  ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par  ......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                    .Treasury bill yields\par  , ..Daily interbank lending rate\par  ...Kenya Bond pricing\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  All Kenyan news.............\par  Kenyan money and debt news...............\par  All Money news.....\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040903e093006ss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
