\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  shilling steady vs dlr after c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2004\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, Aug 27 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shilling        was\par unchanged against the U.S. dollar on Friday, a day after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (CBK) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market and sold\par the greenback to prop up the rapidly weakening local unit.\par  \par     At 0800 GMT leading commercial banks were posting Kenya's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 81.00/20, unchanged from Thursday's closing price.\par     On Thursday CBK Governor Andrew Mullei said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 and importers were concerned by a rapid depreciation in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 price of the shilling, which he blamed on "the intensity of  \par \par \uc2 speculative activities by some local market players".  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, dealers said the bank entered the market and sold  \par \par \uc2 dollars, halting a slide that had seen the shilling touch  \par \par \uc2 historic lows of 83.25/45 versus the dollar on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 By the close of trading on Thursday the local unit had  \par \par \uc2 climbed back to 81.00/20 versus the dollar. Dealers said there  \par \par \uc2 had been little movement in early trading on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The CBK was due to hold a news conference at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has been pretty steady since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said CBK trader Allen Mbindyo. "There is still  \par \par \uc2 underlying demand and there are orders building up below 81."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders said they saw support for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par about 81.40 - 81.50 shillings per dollar.\par     "I don't think the CBK would like the rate to go any higher\par than that," one trader at a major bank told Reuters.\par     The recent slide by the shilling, which had fallen from\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around 79.60 three months ago, has been blamed on several  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 factors including hints by donors that they might pull aid out  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of Kenya over graft allegations and high global oil prices.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                   ............Shilling spot rates\par            ...............Shilling forward rates\par                      .Cross rates\par                ............All Kenya Contributors\par               ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par              ......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                              .Treasury bill yields\par             ,       ..Daily interbank lending rate\par               ...Kenya Bond pricing\par     SPEED GUIDES:\par  \par     RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS:\par     All Kenyan news.............\par     Kenyan money and debt news...............\par     All Money news.....\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040827e08r006ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
