\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Turbulence subsides in forint, zloty.  \b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2004\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint and Polish zloty traded calmer on Thursday after both were whipped around in the previous session on domestic political and economic developments.  \par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling firmed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen entering the market to prop it up after sharp losses against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Hungary's ruling Socialist party selected the charismatic millionaire Ferenc Gyurcsany to be the country's new Prime Minister after he defeated party stalwart Peter Kiss at the party's special congress on Wednesday. After an initial move lower the forint steadied at around 249 per euro . Analysts said the market would probably give Gyurcsany the benefit of the doubt until his policy intentions became clearer.  \par \par \uc2 "Gyurcsany is an unknown and the fact he's an ex-businessman who benefited from early 90s privatisations doesn't necessarily make him a market friendly figure," said Koon Chow, emerging markets strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm still mindful of the Socialist party's low popularity and fearful of further desperate measures they might take to shore that up," he added.  \par \par \uc2 By 0935 GMT, the forint was flat from late Wednesday levels at 249.20 to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Investors have been encouraged by early signs of continuity on budget policy, with a close aide of Gyurcsany's saying that Finance Minister Tibor Draskovics, seen as a key guardian of the fiscal consolidation process in Hungary, would keep his post.  \par \par \uc2 Chow said the forint's high carry - benchmark interest rates are at 11 percent - was also likely to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  well supported in any dips.  \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty jumped to two week highs around 4.3830 against the euro on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market with a bigger-than-expected 50 basis point rate hike, taking key rates to 6.5 percent. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  handed back its gains later on.  \par \par \uc2 "The zloty had gone up after the rate hike but then someone had an order to buy a large amount of euro/polish and that squeezed a few people out the other way," said one London bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 The market retained its weaker bias on Thursday and Chow at CSFB said that could reflect part of a broader trend across the region.  \par \par \uc2 "Technical analysts have been warning for the past three weeks that the strength of central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro is fading and we could be going through a period of weakness. That fits in with the already large positioning in the market."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty traded at 4.4469 per euro  from 4.4349 and at 3.6846 to the\par dollar        from 3.6720.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 KENYA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO DEFEND SHILLING  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Kenyan shilling rose sharply off record lows around 83.25/45 against the dollar hit on Wednesday after dealers reported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement it was taking steps to stabilise the dollar/shilling rate, adding that the shilling's rapid weakening had been caused by speculative pressure applied by domestic players.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers have blamed shilling weakness on a variety of factors, including growing corruption allegations in government which have led to fears donors may desert the country and high global oil prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The shilling bounced to 81 per dollar .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Softer-than-expected South African July producer prices (PPI) offered further vindication for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's shock 50 basis point rate cut earlier this month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July PPI came in at an annual rate of 0.7 percent, below a Reuters poll consensus forecast of 1.3 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rand was little moved on the data, holding steady around 6.67 to the dollar .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040826e08q006q1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
