\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop shilling-traders.   \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2004\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Aug 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, selling dollars to prop the recently weak shilling, traders said.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Andrew Mullei issued a brief statement saying the bank had acted to stabilise the shilling following a rapid decline against the U.S. dollar.    \par \par \uc2  However, the brief statement did not specify what steps the bank had taken.    \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market selling dollars this morning. Clients had been complaining that there was no liquidity and traders had been pushing up the rate saying (dollar) inflows could not match demand," a trader at a major bank said.    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement said it, as well as importers of goods and services, was concerned by the shilling's rapid weakening in recent days.    \par \par \uc2  "To calm the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken steps to stabilise the Kenya shilling exchange rate and ensure that it reflects the true market value of the shilling," Mullei's statement said.    \par \par \uc2  "The major cause of the recent rapid weakening of the shilling against the U.S. dollar has been the intensity of speculative activities by some local market players," he added.    \par \par \uc2  The shilling traded on Thursday at 80.90/81.10 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said, up from a fresh historic low of 83.25/45 shillings hit in early trade on Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered later on Wednesday to about 82.80/83.00.    \par \par \uc2  The recent slide by the shilling, which has fallen from around 79.60 three months ago, has been blamed on several factors including hints by donors that they might pull aid out of Kenya over graft allegations and high global oil prices.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040826e08q005y7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
