\par\par \b \uc2 Kenyan shilling eases slightly on dollar demand.   \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2004\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, Aug 19 (Reuters) - The Kenyan shilling\par weakened marginally against the dollar on Thursday as importers\par from the agriculture, energy and manufacturing sectors bought\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet end of month bills, trader said.\par     At 0950 GMT, leading commercial banks posted the shilling at\par 80.95/81.05 against the greenback compared with Wednesday's\par close of 80.80/81.00.\par     However, the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the\par shilling hit historic lows was expected to keep the local unit\par at around the 80.80/81.00 level, dealer said.\par     "There's some importer demand from maize, energy, even some\par manufacturing companies," said Kennedy Butiko of Bank of Africa\par Kenya.\par     "We're not seeing (the shilling) go beyond 81.00 on fears of\par CBK (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dealers are cautious\par about pushing it beyond that level," he added.\par     CBK Governor Andre Mullei late on Tuesday blamed the\par shilling's recent fall to historic lows on speculation by\par commercial banks.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  He added that the bank would act to ensure the\par shilling was stable and purely determined by demand and supply.\par  \par     A Barclays Bank dealer said importers had suspended their\par orders but were forced to buy dollars as the end of month looms.\par     "Importers believed at 81.00 the shilling (weakness) was\par overdone and were looking for a reversal," he said.\par     Butiko added: "They were forced to make a decision to buy,\par especially the oil sector."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers have blamed a number of factors on the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shilling's fall from donor threats to halt aid to Kenya because   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of rising cases of corruption and high global oil prices to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pending importer demand estimated at $50 million for four   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 million 90-kg bags of maize.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                   ............Shilling spot rates\par            ...............Shilling forward rates\par                      .Cross rates\par                ............All Kenya Contributors\par               ........\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Kenya Index\par              ......Kenyan Bonds contributor pages\par                              .Treasury bill yields\par             ,       ..Daily interbank lending rate\par               ...Kenya Bond pricing\par     SPEED GUIDES:\par  \par     RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS:\par     All Kenyan news.............\par     Kenyan money and debt news...............\par     All Money news.....\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040819e08j00819\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
