\par\par \b \uc2 Ugandan, Tanzanian shillings rise, Kenyan perks up.  \b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2004\par 12:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAIROBI, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Uganda        and Tanzania\par   shillings rose in the week to Wednesday against the\par dollar while the Kenya shilling  began reversing a slide\par to historic lows as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned it might\par step in to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par      Kenya's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Andrew Mullei late on Tuesday\par blamed the local unit's recent fall on speculation by commercial\par banks. He added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would act to ensure the\par shilling rate is stable and purely determined by supply and\par demand.\par  \par     The shilling raced to 80.60/80 to the dollar at Wednesday's\par open from 80.95/81.15 at Tuesday's close.\par     But the local unit gave up some of those gains on the back\par of some light corporate dollar demand. At 1000 GMT it was quoted\par at 80.75/95 to the dollar, dealers said.\par     "Nobody wants to take chances after the CBK (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Kenya\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) threatened to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Moses Kiboi, a\par senior dealer at Citibank.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers of late have blamed the shilling's fall on\par a number of factors including pending importer demand estimated\par at $50 million for 4 million 90-kg bags of maize.\par     Political concerns, donor threats to pull aid from Kenya due\par to rising cases of corruption and high global oil prices have\par kept downward pressure on the shilling as well.\par     Meanwhile, the Tanzania shilling kept strengthening against\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the dollar, buoyed by sustained dollar sales by the Bank of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanzania (BoT) and agricultural exports which dealers expect to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 continue in coming weeks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The shilling's exchange rate stood at 1,080/1,084 shillings  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar compared to 1,084/1,087 shillings at Wednesday's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close of trading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have seen the shilling appreciating on a daily basis.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are a lot of supplies from the agricultural sector and at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the same time, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is selling," Christopher Mutasa,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 treasury manager at the African Banking Corporation said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "It's really going to appreciate if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continue\par selling and with more exporters in the market."\par     Dealers said there was little corporate demand. Some\par surmised the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be selling dollars to reach a\par target of shilling requirements by the end of the quarter.\par     "We don't feel they will be out of the market soon," said\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Marco Samwel, a dealer at Stanbic Bank. "If they were close to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 their target, they would not have allowed the shilling to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthen to this point."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In Uganda, the shilling gained strength against the dollar\par over the week due to low corporate demand for the greenback.\par     At 1000 GMT leading commercial banks were quoting the local\par unit at 1,698/1,700 shillings per U.S. dollar, compared to\par 1,725/1,745 shillings a week ago.\par     "The shilling has continued to rally ... basically on the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 back of absence of corporate dollar demand and significant  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflows of dollars from non-governmental organisations and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 projects," said Moses Elungat, head of trading at Barclays.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the week by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Uganda (BoU) had also boosted the shilling.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sterilised the market on Monday by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the sale side. This triggered off the rally,"\par said Sophie Achak, a trader at Stanbic bank.\par     BoU's "sterilisation" funds are dollars, largely for\par development projects, that it receives from international donors\par and needs to convert into the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Without improved demand for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from corporate\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 clients, traders said they expected the shilling to stabilise at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 levels of around 1,690/1,700 in the days ahead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Daniel Wallis in Kampala and Helen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nyambura in Dar Es Salaam).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040818e08i007yc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
