\par\par \b \uc2 Kenya shilling recovers slightly on c.bank caution.  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2004\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Kenya shilling bounced back marginally in early trade on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor Andrew Mullei late on Tuesday blamed the local unit's recent fall to historic lows on speculation by commercial banks. He added that the bank would act to ensure the shilling is stable and purely determined by demand and supply.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling had raced to 80.60/80 to the dollar at Wednesday's open from 80.95/81.15 at Tuesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 But the local unit gave up some of those gains on the back of some light corporate dollar demand. At 0820 GMT it was quoted at 80.75/95 to the dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Nobody wants to take chances after the CBK (the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Moses Kiboi, a senior dealer at Citibank.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling also received respite after some importers withdrew their orders for dollars when the shilling showed signs of firming, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling has lost 3.8 percent of its value since the beginning of June when it was posted at a mean of 78.87 to the dollar compared to 81.13 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 It has continued to set historic lows in recent weeks which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said was not backed by fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 Ramprasad Hasudi, the treasury manager at Commercial Bank of Africa, said he expected the shilling to strengthen further against the dollar but at a gradual pace because importer demand remained strong while export inflows were sluggish.  \par \par \uc2 "It will take a while because still the demand for dollars is there," he said. "We should not forget grain import is there."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers of late have blamed a number of factors on the shilling's fall, including a pending importer demand estimated at $50 million for 4 million 90-kg bags of maize.  \par \par \uc2 Political concerns, donor threats to pull aid from Kenya due to rising cases of corruption and high global oil prices have kept downward pressure on the shilling as well.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at Imperial Bank said he expected the shilling to trade within a range of 80.60 and 81.10 in the short-term as long as importer demand continues to outweigh supply.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040818e08i0063w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
