\par\par \b \uc2 C.bank steadies Tanzania unit, Uganda,  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  rise.   \b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2004\par 15:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, May 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the Tanzanian shilling largely unchanged against the U.S. dollar in the week to Wednesday, while traders said the Ugandan and Kenyan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had strengthened.   \par \par \uc2 Leading banks in Tanzania's commercial capital Dar es Salaam posted the shilling at 1,115/1,118 per U.S. dollar, compared to 1,116/1,119 a week ago.   \par \par \uc2 "Last week corporates were looking to offload dollars to pay taxes, but the volume was not too big," said Shumbusho Rwezaura, a dealer at Stanbic Bank. "On the other hand, there was demand from all sectors. Whatever inflow came in was snapped up."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Friday at 1,115 shillings each to arrest a decline in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been posted at 1,119 per dollar at the close of trading on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "It appears \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not happy with the volatility caused by customers looking for dollars to make overseas payments," one dealer said, predicting that the shilling would stabilise between 1,113 and 1,120.   \par \par \uc2 The outlook was mixed, with Rwezaura saying he expected the shilling to break the psychological support level of 1,120 if the Bank of Tanzania did not make further dollars sales.   \par \par \uc2 "There is still demand in the office. Businessmen are a bit sceptical of the shilling breaking 1,120, so they are holding back demand. I see no reason why it should not break this level unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Uganda's shilling was stronger against the greenback over the week, trading at 1,890/1,900 shillings per dollar, compared to 1,906/12 shillings last Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the local unit had appreciated because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uganda (BOU) was selling dollars amid low corporate demand.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it is a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lucas Ochieng, a trader at Barclays Bank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gets project funds from donors which they have to disburse."   \par \par \uc2 Outlook was also mixed for the Ugandan unit, with dealers failing to agree on which direction the shilling was headed.   \par \par \uc2 "I think we will see the shilling appreciate because of a lack of demand for dollars and inflows (of dollars) from NGOs," said Joram Ssozi at Standard Chartered bank. "We have also seen some traders selling off their short positions."   \par \par \uc2 Another senior dealer in the capital Kampala said he expected to see the shilling retracing its steps as corporates, particularly from the construction and manufacturing sectors, come looking to buy dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The Kenya shilling also made gains against the dollar. At 1030 GMT banks it was trading at 78.25/45 shillings per dollar, up from 78.35/55 shillings last week.   \par \par \uc2 "Basically the shilling has been very stable this week," said Peter Mwaura, a senior dealer at Credit Agricole Indosuez bank. "There's not been much in the way of inflows (of dollars), and what there has been was matched by demand."   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that in the absence of any market-moving news they saw the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rangebound in the week ahead.   \par \par \uc2 "I think the shilling will basically stay locked between 78.10 and 78.60," said Moses Kiboi at Kenya's Citibank.   \par \par \uc2 "We have tested the 78.50 support level for the shilling this week," said Kihara Maina, a dealer at Barclays Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "There may be one further test, but I think it might hold. On the other hand, I see resistance likely at 77.85."   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Helen Nyambura in Dar es Salaam).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040505e055001sc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
