\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Kenya Cenbank sees stable shilling despite IMF delay.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David Mageria  \par \uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2003\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NAIROBI, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday he expects the shilling to remain stable and competitive despite a decision by the International Monetary Fund to delay a meeting on lending.  \par \par \uc2 The shilling has fallen sharply, weakening to a one-month low after the IMF postponed a meeting on whether to resume lending to the east African country.  \par \par \uc2 At 0730 GMT the shilling was quoted at 78.40/60 to the dollar versus 76.40/76.60 before the news broke that the IMF had postponed the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 In the first official reaction since the shilling's plunge, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Andrew Mullei told Reuters he was confident the IMF would re-open the credit lines adding that the market had read too much into the postponement.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect the shilling to remain stable and competitive despite the postponement of IMF Board discussion on Kenya's request for IMF support," Mullei said in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 "It should be understood that postponement would not in any way imply rejection of the request."  \par \par \uc2 The governor did not give a forecast of what range he expects the shilling to trade. Last month he said the shilling was properly priced when it was posted at between 78.50/70 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Kenyan and IMF officials said an Executive Board meeting in Washington scheduled for November 5 had been delayed until November 21. The Fund said it needed more time for more debt analysis on Kenya.  \par \par \uc2 Mullei said the bank would continue with a policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Unlike the practice previously, CBK (\b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to influence the exchange rate in any way," he said. "With this policy, the shilling has held well against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 The governor admitted that the economy had not recovered "as fast as initially anticipated" due in part to the delay in donor support. But he added he expected a more rapid pick up in 2004 if donors resume lending.  \par \par \uc2 "Economic growth should start accelerating in the medium term," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Kenya's businesses have complained that wrangles in the ruling coalition NARC have dented business confidence and weighed down economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 The governor said the economy registered estimated growth of 1.4 percent in January-July 2003 compared to 0.7 percent for the same period of 2002.  \par \par \uc2 Mullei said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to pursue a low interest rate regime and strive to meet its target of an inflation of less than eight percent despite growing demand by government employees for salary increase.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031030dzau001wq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
