\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Kenya cbank blames foreign banks for shilling fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Macharia \par \uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2002\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Adds governor watching shilling, tells banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  possible, shilling falls further) \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Nov 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday the shilling's fall below a key psychological level was driven by speculation by foreign banks over election worries but he would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at present to stop its fall. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to Reuters in an interview, Nahashon Nyagah added that although there was no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment he was "watching" the shilling and might take action at an appropriate time in the future if banks failed to heed him. \par \par \uc2  "Players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are playing into the hands of foreign banks," Nyagah said. \par \par \uc2  "I have identified the problem is foreign banks from South Africa, Middle East, London and New York. It is not because of fundamental reasons. It is speculative." \par \par \uc2  Nyagah blamed foreign banks for undermining the rate of the shilling based on the perception that Kenya's political future was uncertain due to elections slated for December 27. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reacted to his remarks by pushing the shilling shilling below a nine-year low of 80.10/20 to the dollar hit on Tuesday when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank under the key psychological mark of 80 for the first time in almost a decade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Tuesday's fall was driven by unusually high dollar demand and a dearth of export earnings. At the close on Wednesday it stood at 80.05/25 after briefly touching 80.50/55. \par \par \uc2  In recent months the local unit has stood at about 79.50/55. \par \par \uc2  Kenya holds crucial general elections on December 27 when veteran President Daniel arap Moi is due to step down after 24 years in power, and his ruling party is facing is toughest battle yet against a united opposition. \par \par \uc2  "Electioneering is the excuse," he said. "What uncertainties are there? There is none. Kenya has held elections every five years since independence, and if it is the transition, President Moi has already said he will retire, so there is no uncertainty." \par \par \uc2  Nyagah said he would not use the around $1 billion or 3.4 months cover in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to influence the rate. \par \par \uc2  "I will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Nyagah said, repeating the phrase throughout the interview. \par \par \uc2  He said to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  given present market sentiment would only fuel the unit's slide, and instead urged banks to exercise restraint and not rush to trade at present rates. \par \par \uc2  But the governor offered to sell dollars to individual banks that run into dollar shortfalls. \par \par \uc2  "There is no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment, but I am watching," he said. "I will offer to sell to them (Kenyan banks) dollars at an agreed exchange rate to cover any liquidity shortfall that they have." \par \par \uc2  He said he could meet up to $50 million a day if need be to cover any gaps in their books. \par \par \uc2  He also said that there might come a time when he would contemplate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "At an appropriate time, if the banks do not hear my appeal, I will come in," Nyagah said. \par \par \uc2  DEALERS PREDICT FURTHER FALL \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately to stem the shilling's drop would fuel further speculative buying by foreign banks. \par \par \uc2  "Not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives the speculators the okay to raid the market," said one dealer who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "I'm just surprised that he won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think we shall see the shilling weaken to 81 by Thursday." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they had expected the governor to sell dollars into the market to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge as promised earlier. \par \par \uc2  In late October, the CBK governor told Reuters that the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate below the psychological level of 80 shillings. \par \par \uc2  "Too little too late on verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we have already breached the psychological level of 80," said James Mutuku a senior dealer at \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  Commercial Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hot air, and players now know the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively. The shilling is likely to go into a tailspin." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said it was a positive statement for free markets. \par \par \uc2  "It's a positive statement as it lets the market to determine its own level," Fred Michuki, head of trading at Standard Chartered said. \par \par \uc2  "I think it will turn at the appropriate time, but for now dollar demand will rise because you cannot wish away the political jitters that investors have." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021127dybr00spr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
