\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Kenya cbank blames foreign banks for shilling fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Macharia \par \uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2002\par 13:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Kenya's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday the shilling's fall below a key psychological level was driven by speculation by foreign banks over election uncertainties and added he would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop its fall. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  shilling dipped to a nine-year low on Tuesday, undermined by unusually high dollar demand amid a dearth of export earnings. \par \par \uc2  "Players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are playing into the hands of foreign banks," Nahashon Nyagah told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "I have identified the problem is foreign banks from South Africa, Middle East, London and New York. It is not because of fundamental reasons. It is speculative." \par \par \uc2  At 1230 GMT leading commercial banks posted the shilling at 80.10/20 shillings to the dollar, unchanged from Tuesday's closing levels when it breached the key psychological mark of 80 for the first time in almost a decade. It closed at 79.75/85 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last hit the 80.10 bid level on July 9 1993. \par \par \uc2  The local unit stood at 79.50/60 to the dollar on Wednesday last week. \par \par \uc2  Nyagah blamed foreign banks for undermining the shilling based on the idea that Kenya's political future was uncertain due to elections slated for December 27. \par \par \uc2  Kenya holds crucial general elections on December 27 when veteran President Daniel arap Moi is due to step down after 24 years in power, and his ruling party is facing is toughest battle yet against a united opposition. \par \par \uc2  "Electioneering is the excuse," he said. "What uncertainties are there? There is none. Kenya has held elections every five years since independence, and if it is the transition, President Moi has already said he will retire, so there is no uncertainty." \par \par \uc2  The governor said he would not, for the moment, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the local unit's slide but offered to sell dollars to individual banks that run into dollar shortfalls. \par \par \uc2  "There is no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment, but I am watching," he said. "I will offer to sell to them (Kenyan banks) dollars at an agreed exchange rate to cover any liquidity shortfall that they have." \par \par \uc2  He said he could meet up to $50 million a day if need be to cover any gaps in their books. \par \par \uc2  In late October, the CBK governor told Reuters that the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate below the psychological level of 80 shillings. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not usually reveal when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but the governor has said the bank has not needed to do so in recent times. \par \par \uc2  Nyagah said he would not use the nearly $1 billion or three months cover in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to influence the rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021127dybr00p06\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
