\par\par \b \uc2  Tanzania shilling little changed vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2002\par 12:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The Tanzania shilling was little changed against the dollar on Wednesday compared with a week ago but found support from export earnings, dealers said. The Kenyan shilling eased a touch versus the greenback over the past seven days amid lower tea exports. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT leading commercial banks posted the local unit at 976/977 shillings to the dollar slightly firmer from last Wednesday's close of 977/978. \par \par \uc2  They said Tanzanian shilling gains were expected to continue on export earnings, while the Kenyan shilling struggled back from a three-month low on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The (Tanzanian) shilling has appreciated slightly because it is the peak of the cashew nut and coffee crop season," said Alex Ngusaru at Tanzania's Citibank, adding that there had not been much corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Tanzanian shilling has also been pressured this week by the Bank of Tanzania, which bought dollars in the market on Monday and Tuesday for the second week running to restrain the shilling's rise. \par \par \uc2  "They \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release pressure on the shilling to appreciate," said Ngusaru. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Tanzanian shilling to remain buoyant while \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  shilling was down 10 Kenyan cents overall in the week at 79.10/20 shillings to the greenback from last Wednesday's close of 79.00/10 shillings, but had fought back from low of 79.40/50 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dwindling tea export receipts and a need for dollars by the Kenya Tea Development Agency (KTDA) to make foreign payments hit the shilling. \par \par \uc2  Tea is Kenya's leading \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earner. \par \par \uc2  "The (Kenyan) shilling edged lower to...79.40/50 shillings as tea inflows continue to dwindle, owing to poor weather conditions in August and September," a dealer at Barclays Bank of Kenya said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Kenya shilling to strengthen in the coming week as corporates shy away from dollar buying at present rates and as KTDA's dollar receipts improve. \par \par \uc2  "The shilling is bound to strengthen as inflows come in and as people sitting on dollars sell them to take advantage of the high rates," said the dealer at Barclays bank. \par \par \uc2  "Corporates will then come in to buy dollars at better prices." \par \par \uc2  Traders predicted Kenya's shilling would remain rangebound between 79.10/25 in the coming week. \par \par \uc2  Banks in Uganda were closed on Wednesday as the country is celebrating its independence from British colonial rule. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021009dya900lgl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
