\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS -  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  cen.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  after shilling fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Manoah Esipisu \par \uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1998\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBK) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, selling dollars after a speculative attack forced a sharp fall in the shilling. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, selling some dollars. But the action came late and did not have the desired effect," said a senior dealer at a leading international bank. \par \par \uc2  There was no immediate word from CBK on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers did not say at what rate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars but added that Kenyan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened by up to a shilling against the dollar afterwards. \par \par \uc2  The shilling fell to its lowest level of the day at 64.00/65.50 against the dollar at 3:00 p.m. (1200 GMT), shortly before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before settling at 63.50/64.50. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT, four leading banks had posted the shilling at 62.80/63.35 against the dollar while two other banks were quoting 62.70/63.10 from 62.40/62.90 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There was a speculative attack by some South African banks, they hit the market on Friday and this morning and returned later to take their profits," one treasurer told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said that the market remained nervous and there was a possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Tuesday to stem any further shilling declines. \par \par \uc2  "There are just a few South Africans playing around the market and influencing the frenetic movement of the last few hours," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the huge spreads - between a shilling and 1.50 shillings - reflected the nervous state of the market. They added that it was too early to say what direction the shilling would take due to uncertainty on further CBK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, dealers said a decline in treasury bill yields had forced a complimentary decline in the shilling rate. \par \par \uc2  "The steady decline in interest rates on treasury bills is putting pressure on the local unit," Chris Rengo, chief dealer at Standard Chartered Bank, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The average yield on Kenya's benchmark 91-day treasury bill fell to 12.959 percent last Thursday from 14.349 percent the previous week. The 12-week moving average of the 91-day T-bill yield fell to 18.330 percent, from 19.113 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said unrelenting corporate demand supported by some interest for dollars from offshore banks had convinced exporters to hold on to their dollars, hoping to offload when the greenback is at its peak. \par \par \uc2  They said sentiment was for a weaker shilling. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said he had noted demand for dollars from the oil sector with players looking to buy crude oil at the current very low prices. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a shilling opening mean indicative rate of 62.3461 to the dollar from 61.6683 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  ((Nairobi newsroom, +254 2 330261/2 fax +254 2 338860, nairobi.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duce02eif\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pn