\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya shilling steady in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, March 20 (Reuters) - The Kenya shilling hovered at just under 60 to the dollar on Friday in a balanced market with thin trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said there was evidence the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  snapped up anything offered stronger than 60 to the dollar on Thursday in an attempt to curb any rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is coming in at anything below 60 and that is the only thing stopping us having a very strong shilling by now," said the dealer, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could go as high as 58. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said he understood the Bank had bought $15 million on Thursday and it was checking the market again on Friday but had yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "They are trying to prevent it going below (stronger than) 60, because that would hurt exporters and agriculture and tourism which have already been very hard hit," said the dealer. Other dealers said they saw no hard evidence of bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Factors connected to rising taxes and perceptions of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy have made 60 shillings to the dollar a difficult threshold for the shilling to cross. \par \par \uc2  Dealer said they were trading in the 59.95/60.20 range but spreads could widen slightly, with buyers prepared to accept variations in an effort to close business quickly in advance of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya put the mean indicative shilling rate against the dollar on Thursday at 60.1222, which traders said was the week's only busy day. \par \par \uc2  "The shilling gained marginal ground on the dollar yesterday (Thursday) as exporter proceeds poured into the market. Traders have involuntarily been building up long dollar positions over the week due to whimsical demand from importers," Citibank said in a report on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Money market lending rates stood at around 23-24 percent on Friday, up from 21 percent on Thursday after having drifted upwards all week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ((Matthew Bigg, Nairobi newsroom, +254 2 330261/2 fax +254 2 338860, nairobi.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du3k092b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
