\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  as shilling surges. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wambui Chege \par \uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Jan 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market on Tuesday buying dollars to stem a rapid appreciation of the shilling which dealers said was an apparent vote of confidence in new finance minister Simeon Nyachae. \par \par \uc2  "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen in the market to support the shilling," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at an international bank said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made no comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Monday's pledge by Nyachae to continue economic reforms launched by his predecessor Musalia Mudavadi had calmed market nerves and ended market uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "I have no intention of altering the (reform) programme my colleague had started. The reforms were based on endorsement of the cabinet and government of which both of us are members," Nyachae said at a formal hand-over ceremony. \par \par \uc2  "Nyachae's statement was shilling positive and gave the market assurance," one senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The shilling picked up steam late Tuesday afternoon after breaking the 62.00 resistance level in early trade, commercial bank dealers said. \par \par \uc2  By 4.10 p.m. local time (1310 GMT) it was quoted at around 60.00/61.00 to the dollar, from an opening mid-rate of 62.2944, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At one point, the bid rate fell as low as 59.50 before the market pulled back slightly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Today we had a fair amount of dollars from offshore investors -- about $5-$10 million," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The shilling appreciated partly because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably slow to participate in the market and nobody wanted to hold the market alone," he added. \par \par \uc2  But although the shilling looks set to carve out more gains in the absence of significant demand for dollars, dealers said they were taking no risks and would maintain wide spreads. \par \par \uc2  Spreads between bid and offer rates widened to over a shilling on Tuesday from around 20 cents on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Kenya's financial markets remain untouched by turmoil in Asian markets -- and have been on a recovery path since the general elections two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The Nairobi Stock Exchange 20-share index has gained ground every day so far this year. It closed at 3307.07 on Tuesday and is now 6.2 percent up on the year. \par \par \uc2  ((Nairobi newsroom,  +254 2 330261/2  fax +254 2 338860, nairobi.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07xo0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
