\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya c.bank buys dlrs to stem shilling's rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars to stem the shilling's rise, commercial bank dealers said \par \par \uc2  "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen in the market to support the shilling," one leading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at an international bank said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made no comment. \par \par \uc2  The Kenyan shilling rallied strongly on Tuesday in an apparent vote of confidence for new Finance Minister Simeon Nyachae. \par \par \uc2  By 3.40 p.m. local time (1240 GMT) it was quoted at around 60.00/61.00 to the dollar, from an opening mid-rate of 62.2944, dealers said. At one point, the bid rate fell as low as 59.50 before the market pulled back slightly, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Monday's pledge by Nyachae to continue economic reforms launched by his predecessor Musalia Mudavadi had calmed market nerves and ended market uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  "Nyachae's statement was shilling positive and gave the market assurance," one senior dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The shilling picked up steam after breaking the 62.00 resistance level in early trade, commercial bank dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ((Wambui Chege, Nairobi newsroom,  +254 2 330261/2  fax +254 2 338860, nairobi.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07xmb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
