n. The country's trade deficit reached 8% of gross domestic product in 1996. \par \par \uc2  But the suspension of the loan was the trigger for the shilling's collapse, and analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's salvation also depends on the IMF. \par \par \uc2  'I can't see the shilling recovering without some form of package in place internationally,' said Douch. \par \par \uc2  The Fund is likely to insist on steps to combat corruption that President Daniel arap Moi may be unwilling to take. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1544GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8805vok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
