\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Braces For Further Shilling Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 1997\par 10:31\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI (Dow Jones)--The Kenyan \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was Thursday braced for further shilling declines, following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.6% drop against the dollar Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Thursday at 66.50/68.50 shillings, up from Wednesday's closing at 65.90/68.00, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya said. \par \par \uc2  "It's still early in the day. We're watching carefully... It depends on what orders come," Charles Musawo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the trend will be clearer at noon local time (0900 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The shilling's 4.6% fall on Wednesday brought its decline since Thursday to 13.6%. \par \par \uc2  There were bids as low as 69 shillings per dollar on Wednesday morning. The shilling's lowest level stands at 69.22 in October 1993. \par \par \uc2  The shilling's recovery from earlier lows followed comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which said it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the shilling, and called for calm. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wishes to re-affirm that it will continue to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as and when justified," \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central\par Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Micah Cheserem said.\par  - -   -(AP-DJ-08-07-97 0830GMT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT  07-08-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0831GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt87009br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
