\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya central bank \highlight\uc2  calls for calm,  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, Aug 6 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called for an end to panic on Nairobi's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the shilling's slide by selling dollars. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya Governor Micah Cheserem urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to trade "in an orderly manner so that losses arising from the panic and speculative transactions would be minimised". \par \par \uc2  Commercial bank dealers said following his statement the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling at least $10 million. \par \par \uc2  "The shilling exchange rate to the U.S. dollar opened at a mean rate of 64 and rapidly depreciated to a selling rate as low as 69...the speed of depreciation is worrying," Cheserem said. \par \par \uc2  He said commercial banks reported that several importers were rushing to pay their foreign bills in order to minimise exchange losses while exporters were holding back dollars in anticipation of further shilling losses. \par \par \uc2  In a statement, Cheserem also said foreign investors in government treasury bills and stocks were in the market after the IMF halted a key loan package to Kenya on Thursday, buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to repatriate their investments. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8601jhk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picsc