\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya Shilling Recovers, But Still Closes Down 4.6% \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1997\par 16:32\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NAIROBI (Dow Jones)--The Kenyan shilling recovered from a sharp drop against the dollar earlier Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1300 GMT, the shilling closed at 65.90/68.00 to the dollar, up from 69.00 to the dollar earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Kenya said. \par \par \uc2  The shilling's 4.6% fall for the day brought its decline since Thursday to 13.6%. \par \par \uc2  The shilling's sharp decline followed the International Monetary Fund's decision Thursday to suspend a $220 million loan to the country. The IMF said it had taken the step because Kenya hadn't taken sufficient steps to meet its concerns about corruption and management of the energy sector. \par \par \uc2  The shilling's recovery from earlier lows followed comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which said it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the shilling, and called for calm. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wishes to re-affirm that it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as and when justified," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Micah Cheserem said. \par \par \uc2  Charles Musawo, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday, but provided no further details. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT  06-0