\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  Cen Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to stem shilling fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wambui Chege \par \uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 1997\par 12:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, July 11 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBK) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to stem the shilling fall on continued jitters after political unrest early in the week, Governor Micah Cheserem said. \par \par \uc2  Cheserem said the shilling rate versus the dollar had eased to as low as 61.50 for bids from around 55 at the beginning of the week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered $19 million to the market and there were few takers, he told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The CBK posted opening rates for the day at 57.61 against the dollar compared to 56.38 on Thursday. Against the pound, the shilling was posted at a commercial mean of 97.27 from 95.10. \par \par \uc2  Nine people were killed in Kenya on Monday during the most violent clashes between police and protesters since a violent campaign in July 1990 that helped persuade Moi to allow multi-party politics. \par \par \uc2  The violent protests have upset investors and made many wary of this emerging market. Turnover on the Nairobi stock exchange has slumped to a year's low. \par \par \uc2  Commercial bank dealers posted rates in the 59-61 range and maintained spreads as wide as three shillings. Signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it had more dollars than market demand was expected to calm market nerves and see shilling gains. \par \par \uc2  The shilling was poised to recoup some losses, they said. \par \par \uc2  "There has been overeaction in the market," Cheserem said, adding that quoted rates for the shilling were ridiculous. \par \par \uc2  The shilling last touched the 60 range and threatened further losses versus the dollar in October 1993. \par \par \uc2  Bank dealers said Thursday's move from 56.30 to a close as low as 59.30 against the dollar had sent waves of panic in the market, which they thought was an overreaction. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in the market this morning and we do not have any takers," a treasurer from a top bank said. \par \par \uc2  Cheserem, 47, who is one of Kenya's leading economic reform leaders, said one bank asked for $5 million but took only $1 million when the bank said it would meet the demand. \par \par \uc2  Another official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said state utility Kenya Power & Lighting Corp asked for $6.5 million but then backed down after the bank also said it would meet the demand. \par \par \uc2  Cheserem said the market would calm as both sides of Kenya's political divide settled their differences. "The biggest word in town is dialogue. Dialogue in block letters." \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the week, commercial dealers said the market had become so nervous that they feared the shilling would not be able to recoup its losses without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7b02oct\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
