\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Kenya \highlight\uc2  shilling down on dollar after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, May 8 (Reuter) - The Kenyan shilling lost marginally against the dollar after a second day of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commercial dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week followed a month of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  absence from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted a commercial mean rate of 53.90 against the dollar compared to 53.89 on Wednesday, while against the pound, it was posted at a mean rate of 87.41 from 88.15. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot inflows coming into the market and they (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are the only ones buying," a dealer from a leading commercial bank told Reuters. "Actually, they are the ones holding rates at this level." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the shilling was holding steady trading at 53.80/54 but added that the underlying tone for the shilling was still bullish -- at least for the short term. \par \par \uc2  The money market continued tight on Thursday with overnight rates quoted at 20 percent unchanged. \par \par \uc2  --Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5805ts6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
