\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya shilling weakens against dollar, pound. \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, May 15 (Reuter) - The Kenyan shilling weakened against the dollar and sterling at the close on Monday, commercial bank traders said. \par \par \uc2  The shilling closed at a commercial bank mean rate of 53.50 against the dollar, down 1.20 from its opening at 52.30 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The shilling also weakened against the pound at the close, trading at a commercial bank mean rate of 83.50 from 80.47 at open on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Musalia Mudavadi said on Sunday the government would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which began a dramatic fall on April 27 from the level of about 44, which it had held for six months. \par \par \uc2  "We have left the shilling to market forces and these must determine its movement. There will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence its performance," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  Television Network (KTN) quoted Mudavadi as saying. \par \par \uc2  "But a (shilling) fall is normal movement and it should not cause unnecessary panic," he added. \par \par \uc2  The fall in the shilling has been attributed to a surge in demand for dollars from oil companies and other commercial importers. \par \par \uc2  Economists say tourist receipts are down in the current low season and fears that Western donors will take measures against Kenya over the pace of economic and political reforms at a conference in July have also caused market jitters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has taken on a marginal role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since February 28, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday and Thursday by selling dollars. Overall, it did not prevent the shilling from falling further by week's end. \par \par \uc2  Some economic analysts have predicted the shilling will stabilise at 50 to the dollar, but others argue that 55 would be a more natural level. Exporters have long argued that the shilling was overvalued at 44 and was hurting their business. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5f07rb4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
