\par\par \b \uc2  Kenya shilling strengthens against dollar, pound. \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, May 15 (Reuter) - The Kenyan shilling firmed against the dollar and sterling despite comments from Finance Minister Musalia Mudavadi that the government would not shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been falling steadily since April 27. \par \par \uc2  "We have left the shilling to market forces and these must determine its movement. There will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence its performance," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  Television Network (KTN) quoted Mudavadi as saying late on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  At Monday's opening session of trading, the shilling was quoted at a commercial bank mean rate of 52.30 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up 20 cents from Friday's closing rate of 52.50. \par \par \uc2  The shilling also strengthened against the pound, trading at 80.47 from 81.67 at close on Friday. \par \par \uc2  It had been falling since April 27, when it was quoted at around 44 per dollar, a level it had held for some six months. \par \par \uc2  "A (shilling) fall is normal movement and it should not cause unnecessary panic," Mudavadi said. \par \par \uc2  The fall in the shilling has been atributed to a surge in demand for dollars from oil companies and commercial importers. \par \par \uc2  Economists say tourist receipts are also down in the current low season. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBK), which has taken on a marginal role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since February 28, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Monday and Thursday, selling dollars, but it did not prevent the shilling from falling further by week's end. \par \par \uc2  Some economic analysts have predicted the shilling would stabilise at 50 to the dollar, but others argue that 55 would be a more natural level. Exporters have long argued that the shilling was overvalued at 44 and was hurting business. \par \par \uc2  -- Nairobi Newsroom + 254 2 330-261. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5f07r9z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
