\par\par \b \uc2  Nairobi bourse chief warns against strong shilling. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Matt Bigg \par \uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NAIROBI, April 12 (Reuter) - The head of the Nairobi bourse said on Wednesday a strong international shilling was hurting business and contributing to losses incurred by leading blue chips on his market. \par \par \uc2  Jimnah Mbaru said most of the blue chip companies "attribute their reduced profits and generally poor results to a strong shilling". \par \par \uc2  "A \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy influenced primarily by market forces of supply and demand....has resulted in a strong Kenya shilling which has had a major impact on the economy as a whole." \par \par \uc2  To combat the overvalued shilling Mbaru advocated new government action. \par \par \uc2  "We would like to call upon the government to adopt a Managed Exchange Rate Policy (MERP) whereby $1 is stabilised around 55.00 Kenya shillings," he said in a speech to Nairobi's Rotary club. \par \par \uc2  "If properly implemented this policy could enable Kenya's economy to grow by at least 5 percent per annum." \par \par \uc2  Monetary Stabilisation Bonds (MSB's) could be used to mop up any excess money supply from the economy, he said in an effort to quell policymakers' worries that the MERP could lead to renewed inflation. \par \par \uc2  And it would "curb massive dumping and help to strengthen the local manufacturing sector and in particular the textile sector", he said. \par \par \uc2  Companies such as Brooke Bond Kenya, Sasini Tea & Coffee, Limuru Tea, Bamburi Portland Cement and Kakuzi showed a marked drop in profits in their last reports, Mbaru said. \par \par \uc2  Limuru Tea saw profits fall 66 percent from 68.2 million shillings to 22.9 million shillings. \par \par \uc2  Kenya needed a managed exchange rate policy because companies attributed falling profits to the strength of the shilling against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He quoted C. A. Ouda a director of Brooke Bond Kenya as explaining the company's 55 percent drop in profits in terms of "the appreciation of the Kenya shilling against the dollar". \par \par \uc2  To sustain the policy the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Kenya\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as necessary to ensure the shilling stabilises at the correct rate, Mbaru said. \par \par \uc2  In 1993 the Kenyan government freed interest rates, removed import and export restrictions and abolished price controls on key commodities. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4c08ozn\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (kenya near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs 